(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [11 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [12 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [13 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [15 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [21 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [22 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [23 1 "// or Repl."] [45 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [48 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [49 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [82 1 "// unsupportedOperation is io.UnsupportedOperation's stand-in until _pyio (PY6): a ValueError (its base, with OSError)."] [85 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [101 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [176 1 "// The standard streams' buffer (PY6e's REQUEST: subprocess's children write sys.stdout.buffer): a binary"] [177 1 "// view of the same bufio reader or writer, so text and bytes keep their order."] [274 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [295 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [341 25 "// types.SimpleNamespace (PY6b: FrozenImporter makes them)"] [343 54 "// pyi's own .pyc files (PY6b): __pycache__/NAME.arbace-314.pyc, its own magic number"] [348 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): a namespace standing in for the struct sequence"] [360 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, as namespaces of CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [391 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): the tools' registry and the events' numbers; no event is ever raised (pyi has no"] [392 2 "// instrumentation yet: the debugging family's)"] [463 43 "// PY6c"] [466 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [467 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [529 5 "// traceback objects are PY5b's (a Traceback is not an Object yet)"] [539 26 "// -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [582 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [640 3 "// dataclasses' slots=True (gh-135228): __dict__ and __weakref__ taken out of a heap type's dict"] [658 2 "// get_asyncgen_hooks and set_asyncgen_hooks (sysmodule.c; asyncio's event loops set theirs around run_forever):"] [659 2 "// the running thread's hooks, a sys.asyncgen_hooks; an argument left out keeps its hook, None clears it"] [693 2 "// _PySys_SetIntMaxStrDigits: 0 (no limit) or at least 640, sys.flags.int_max_str_digits with it (queue 202: a no-op,"] [694 2 "// so test_decimal's PyCoverage, which sets 7000, met the 4300 digits' limit)"] [721 2 "// threading.settrace_all_threads and setprofile_all_threads: no-ops as settrace and setprofile (tracing is"] [722 2 "// PY5e's); missing, they raised before the test released its waiting thread, which then hung the exit"] [736 24 "// its functions' __module__ \"sys\" (PY6f's REQUEST 8, as importBuiltin tags the others)"] [740 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [741 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [758 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [766 1 "// writeTo writes s to a file object: the interpreter's stdout when f is nil or None, a textFile directly,"] [767 1 "// else f.write(s)."] [788 1 "// exactArgsN checks a function's call: n positional arguments, no keywords (CPython's messages)."] [802 1 "// cpythonSizeof is sys.getsizeof as CPython 3.14 answers it on a 64-bit build for the core immutable types"] [803 1 "// and the list and tuple (the list's allocation taken as its length), 0 for any other object (PY6b's"] [804 1 "// request: test_marshal sizes its big-memory tests by sys.getsizeof of an int at import)."] [843 1 "// versionInfoType is sys.version_info's struct sequence (PY6b's request: test_importlib reads its releaselevel):"] [844 1 "// a tuple with the fields' names."] [881 1 "// asyncgenHooks are each thread's async generator hooks (firstiter, finalizer; nil unset, None too), as the thread"] [882 1 "// state's async_gen_firstiter and async_gen_finalizer: firstiter called on an async generator's first __anext__, asend,"] [883 1 "// athrow or aclose (coro.go's asyncGenInitHooks; asyncio's tracking of unfinished async generators for"] [884 1 "// shutdown_asyncgens); the finalizer kept, never called (pyi has no finalization, PY7)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[120 53] [138 30] [201 54] [219 34] [267 30] [297 48] [363 13] [363 26] [449 20] [491 62] [497 62] [511 26] [518 54] [521 26] [527 26] [528 43] [542 51] [552 56] [558 43] [561 46] [573 7] [573 30] [587 31] [621 34] [634 62] [641 68] [652 41] [661 63] [700 28] [751 63] [760 48] [776 28]]} (go/file "sys.go" :imports [


